From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andriy Chuma <chuma.andriy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:55:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] m68k: Add the Create Flippies PC machine

The Create Flippies PC is a 68040 computer emulated by the Create Flippies
mod for Minecraft. It has its own devices, mapped at the top of the
physical address space: a system controller, an interrupt controller with
31 level-sensitive lines, an interval timer counting microseconds, three
16550 COM ports, disks, a network card, three framebuffers and two PS/2
ports.

Add it as machine type MACH_FLIPPIES (15), selected by CONFIG_FLIPPIES:

- head.S maps 0xff000000 and up one to one with ITT1 and DTT1, as the
  virt machine does, so the framebuffers, devices and boot ROM need no
  page tables, and ioremap() hands those addresses back unchanged. Early
  output goes to COM1.
- Every interrupt controller line stays routed to output 0, which reaches
  the CPU as autovector level 4. Its handler asks CLAIM for the lowest
  pending and enabled line until there is none; line n is irq 8 + n,
  masked and unmasked through ENABLE.
- The interval timer's 64-bit microsecond counter is the clocksource and
  sched_clock; its countdown, periodic or one-shot, is the clock event
  device, limited to one second so that timekeeping's catch-up after a
  long tickless idle stays short.
- Reset and power off go through the system controller.
